The pickaxe does d6/d3 damage. +2 for expert skill. A dwarvish mattock would
be d12+2/d8+2d6+2. Snick at basic katana skill is d10+d8/d12+d8. The
pickaxe is right out. The mattock would have +2 to-hit bonus (expert skill
- built-in malus), while snick has +1, but you should still be hitting
enough with Snickersnee. The average damage against small/large monsters
would be 8.5/13.5 for the mattock and 10/11 for Snickersnee, if I'm not
mistaken, so it's a close call. You might want to stick to a mattock until
you get to Gehennom, where it might get cursed, and reserve the skill slots
for Grayswandir.

